<!-- COMPARISON: FLUTTER, REACT NATIVE, COMPOSE MULTIPLATFORM -->
<section id="compare" class="prose-section">
  <div class="site-container">
    <p class="prose-eyebrow">Positioning &middot; Framework comparison</p>
    <h2 class="prose-h2">Where Osprey Native stands among CMP, Flutter, and React Native</h2>
    <p class="prose-lead">
      You should not have to choose between authentic platform widgets and a GPU canvas &mdash; or accept a JavaScript engine
      or JVM on desktop just to share code.
    </p>

    <div tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="compare-caption" class="table-wrapper">
      <table class="compare-table">
        <caption id="compare-caption">Architectural comparison: Osprey Native vs. Compose Multiplatform (CMP), Flutter, and React Native</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Capability</th>
            <th scope="col" class="col-osprey">Osprey Native</th>
            <th scope="col">Compose Multiplatform (CMP)</th>
            <th scope="col">Flutter</th>
            <th scope="col">React Native</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Rendering model</th>
            <td class="col-osprey"><strong>Both:</strong> real native controls (SwiftUI, WinUI, Android) <strong>OR</strong> FerroUI / GPUI GPU canvas</td>
            <td>Skia canvas for shared UI (native views require platform interop wrappers)</td>
            <td>Impeller / Skia canvas only (framework-drawn widget copies)</td>
            <td>Native platform views only (custom GPU scenes need native modules)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Runtime &amp; compilation</th>
            <td class="col-osprey">LLVM AOT native machine code everywhere + WebAssembly on web; no JS engine, no JVM</td>
            <td>Kotlin/Native on iOS, JVM on desktop &amp; Android, Wasm/JS on web</td>
            <td>Dart AOT on mobile &amp; desktop, JS/Wasm on web</td>
            <td>JavaScript engine (Hermes) + JSI / native bridge</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Reactivity</th>
            <td class="col-osprey">Compiler-derived <code>Signal&lt;T&gt;</code> &amp; keyed regions from the ground up</td>
